From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Nov 20 22:58:49 2001
From: "Gilbert, Ashley" <Ashley.Gilbert () eadvancemed ! com>
Date: Tue, 20 Nov 2001 22:58:49 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Audit subsystem install - kernel config
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653643321884

To the get the system back on the network so I could remotely log in:

# init 3 =3D=3D> bring her to multi-user mode
# ifconfig =3D=3D> reconfigured nic cards
# /sbin/init.d/inetd start =3D=3D> Starts network services
# /usr/sbin/route add network Gateway =3D=3D> manually add routes

Thanks to Raul Sossa.  He pointed me to the "Change your hostname
permanently" document from Compaq, so when I reboot I won't have to do
it all again...always a plus. =20
The problem was I needed to change the first line of the system
configuration file (/usr/sys/conf/HOSTNAME), ident, to my current
hostname.=20
# sed -e "s/OLDNAME/NEWNAME/" OLDNAME > NEWNAME
# rm OLDNAME

Thanks,
Ashley


