To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Postfix in TruCluster
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653643321847


Well I didn't get any replies on this one!
I guess no-one is using postfix as the MTA in a TruCluster.

However the folks at postfix-users were able to help, and I was able to
verify that postfix works fine in a TruCluster when using the 'flock' file
locking option.

> Use the "postlock" command.
>
>     postlock /var/spool/mail/mumble sleep 1000
>
> It has options to play with different locking styles. YOu can run
> multiple postlock processes and see if they recognize each other's
> locks, and if your mail reading software recognizes those locks.
>

Thanks Wietse,

That works very well. I've verified that flock works perfectly in
preventing concurrent delivery to mbox from different cluster members, as
well as locking out impad and popd :)

Postfix is great.

Paul

