From tru64-unix-managers  Sat Nov 17 19:02:40 2001
From: Thomas Leitner <tom () radar ! tu-graz ! ac ! at>
Date: Sat, 17 Nov 2001 19:02:40 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: AlphaServer DS20E, Power Supplies.
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653643321829


Hi,

The consensus of all replies is: There's only one power connector and
only one power cord shared between the three PSUs. Additionally there
must be two PSUs operating simultaneously to have the system running.
As soon as the number of live PSUs drops below two, the systems powers
down.

I also found the complete hardware docs of the DS20E at:

       http://www.compaq.com/alphaserver/ds20e/ds20e_tech.html

