that when I do an "su passport" I get in, but I'm in the root directory. =
 When I simply type "cd"  it says /star/passport not found.  Which is =
interesting in that /star/passport is the home directory of the user =
passport on our Production servers.  So my question is, where else can a =
home directory be specified other than the passwd file.  We use the =
/var/yp/src passwd file (and yes, there is only one entry for the user =
passport), and I also double checked and made sure that the /etc/passwd =
