Ok...partly user error, partly network guys (yes! again!!).  the user =
error was on my part...I guess it would help to put the NEW IP address =
of the slave server in my DNS settings--not the old one.  Once I did =
that everything internal was working.  I still couldn't get external DNS =
names to resolve.  Talked to the network guys, and they mentioned that =
they had changed some router settings so that none of the servers =
(except the master DNS server) can get to the outside world.  Not the =
best thing for a slave dns server, but that's the way it was intended.  =
So really...i have no problems at all (with DNS anyway).  Which is good =
being I only received one reply.  Thanks anyway to the un-named "system =
administration account" person who tried to help. =20

Jonathan Williams
