Hi Admins:

The solution to my problem was as follows:

I got totally back on track simply by using the command:

/usr/local/samba/bin/smbpasswd -a username

this reenters the userid back into the smbpasswd file.

it then asks you for a new password(which I entered) and I was able to
connect to the shares normally. 

 

I would like to thank Michael Acklin and Tony Brown.

 

Original question:

Hello Managers:

I am trying to add more users to the SMB passwd file so SAMBA recognizes the

passwords. It is my understanding that this is done by the following

command:

cat /etc/passwd | mksmbpasswd > /usr/local/samba/private/smbpasswd

Can anyone enlighten me on this subject, that is, how to add more clients so

SAMBA recognizes network clients, userids, and passwords. I am running

SAMBA-2.0.5a. Thanks...

 

 

 

 

