All,

I've connected a UPS to our ES40 server and installed CheckUPS 11 monitoring
software. The UPS is monitored through a cable connection to the 9 pin
serial port on the back of the server, however during configuration you have
to specify the device name for this serial port. If I take the default
(/dev/tty00) it can't see the UPS and the same applies if I enter the
recommened device name from the installation notes (/dev/tty1b), this
doesn't exist !

Can anyone advise how I can establish the exact device name for the 9 pin
serial port on the ES40 ?

These are the options :-

[canada]/dev $ ls tty* 
tty    ttyp1  ttyp5  ttyp9  ttypd  ttyq1  ttyq5  ttyq9  ttyqd
tty00  ttyp2  ttyp6  ttypa  ttype  ttyq2  ttyq6  ttyqa  ttyqe
tty01  ttyp3  ttyp7  ttypb  ttypf  ttyq3  ttyq7  ttyqb  ttyqf
ttyp0  ttyp4  ttyp8  ttypc  ttyq0  ttyq4  ttyq8  ttyqc

Regards,
Mike

 

