All,

Bit late but here is what you need to do or at least what I needed to do.
Boot from CD, drop into unix shell, make the domains and filesets, mount
these new domains, restore from the backup. Whilst in this mode I had to
remove all entries for LSM, (remove /etc/vol*, /dev/vol/*, /dev/rvol/*,
entries from /etc/inittab etc... effectively getting rid of LSM from the new
system. Shutdown the server and reboot from the disk you did the restore to,
and then reinstall LSM. 

The error message that is was receiving below was a bit of a red herring as
I believe that it refers to the ethernet card somehow.

Thanks to Jason Neil and John Farmer for their assistance, also Peter
Reynolds, Tom Kemp, Lucien Hercaud and Alan @ nabeth.

Cheers

Steve

