From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Nov 13 14:08:13 2001
From: david.humphreys () cht20 ! co ! uk
Date: Tue, 13 Nov 2001 14:08:13 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Cluster and RIP problem
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653643321741



We are having problems with gated daemon on our clustered servers advertising
routes through it's memory channel for local addresses, which causes all sorts
of connectivity problems. The problems seems to lie around the
/etc/gated.conf.xxx files.

The standard /gated.conf appears to be set correctly, with RIP set in Quiet
Mode. The /etc/gated.conf.member1 appears to be set to broadcast over ethernet,
a private FDDI ring and memory channel. The /etc/gated.conf.member2 is set to
broadcast over FDDI and memory channel only. The comment section of these two
files states that they are created by aliasd and that we should not edit them.

Any ideas how we can resolve this problem?

Thanks,

Dave

From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Nov 13 13:59:32 2001
From: Russ_Fish () idx ! com
Date: Tue, 13 Nov 2001 13:59:32 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Tru64 and DBD-Oracle and CGI
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653643321739

Thanks to:

"Christoph Klein" <christoph.klein@ucpag.com>
"Nemholt, Jesper Frank" <JesperFrank.Nemholt@compaq.com>

I've included Christopher's response below:

...you have to insert the following lines in your apache httpd.conf:

SetEnv LD_LIBRARY_PATH "/opt/oracle/product/8.1.6/lib"
SetEnv LD_RUN_PATH "/opt/oracle/product/8.1.6/lib"
SetEnv NLS_LANG "AMERICAN_AMERICA.UTF8"
SetEnv NLS_DATE_FORMAT "YYYY-MM-DD HH24:MI:SS"
SetEnv ORACLE_HOME "/opt/oracle/product/8.1.6"

(of course you have to alter the path, the date & the character format
to fit your needs ;-)

if you run fast cgis then you also have to pass some of the variables:

for example via:

FastCGIConfig -restart -restart-delay 10 -idle-timeout 90
-maxClassProcesses 1 -initial-env LD_LIBRARY_PATH -initial-env
ORACLE_HOME

-----Original Message-----
