have been a file still in use (or open) at the time of deletion.  Only =
after the file is "closed" with the space actually be freed up.  This =
sounds alright, except for the fact that the directory I deleted was an =
export of an informix database (creates a directory, and converts the =
whole database into ASCII text files which is what is in the directory). =
 These files would only be used during an import of an informix =
database.  there were no imports running at the time I deleted this =
directory (I wasn't doing one, and I'm the only one who knows how to do =
one).  So it remains a mystery as to why the system thought one or more =
of those files were open, but at least now I have somewhere to look if =
this happens again.  Thanks for the many responses.

