Subject: SUMMARY: CPU lincense update
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653643321601



Hello,

ok this is how you doit , thanks to Arrigu Triulzi and Tom Blinn:

first install the new license with
# lmf register
...

then delete the temporary one:
# lmf delete osf-base dec  <authorisation number>

then do a reset
# lmf reset

and with a
# lmf list full for osf-base

you can see the new license is working!

Also thanks to Wofram Kraft who pointed out that the old license doesnt
need to be
deleted. But eversince the temporary license expires on December the 24th I
wanted
to be sure i dont need it ;-)

Have fun
Samier.




                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
